  <h2 class="h2">Directions for the next 2 (two) items:</h2>
  <div class="comprehension">
    <div class="comprehension-intro">Read the following passage and answer the items that follow. Your answers should be based solely on the passage.</div>
    <h3 style="text-align:center;">Passage</h3>
    <p>How is deflation done? Most countries use a method called ‘double deflation’, where input and output prices are deflated separately. Consider a manufacturer importing oil for use in production. If oil prices fall, output prices do not and quantities remain the same, real value added should not change. But if the same deflator is used for inputs and outputs, as in India, it would look as if the manufacturer had become more productive.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="card" data-correct="a">
<ul class="breadcrumbs">
